An independent, open-source Android app to control Google Pixel Buds Pro 2 — fully offline: no Google Play services needed, no `INTERNET` permission, no location permission, no account.

**Features:** noise control (Noise cancellation, Adaptive, Transparency, Off) and a Quick Settings tile — with "Changed by the Buds" in its details when a bud's press-and-hold or the Buds themselves changed the mode while the noise-control tab is open · equalizer with presets and Volume EQ · battery Left/Right (with charging), the Case and a "probably worn" line · Find My Buds (ring Left / Right) · touch controls, press and hold per bud and its noise-control modes · head gestures, Multipoint, conversation detection, in-ear detection · balance (finer near the centre), mono audio · case sounds and dark mode on gear → Settings · firmware and serial numbers on gear → Info.

**New in 1.2.1:** a **Noise-control channel** setting on gear → Settings for phones with Google Play services, where Play's Fast Pair takes the channel back about 5 seconds after this app opened it on the noise-control tab — "Show a hint, do not take it back" (the default: the noise-control card says when it was taken) or "Take it back while the noise-control tab is open" (3, 6 and 12 seconds later, three times per visit of the tab, then the hint); without Play services nothing changes.

**Known issues in 1.2.1:** in a user with Google Play services, with "Show a hint" every press-and-hold after the first (about 5 seconds after a connect or a tap) reaches Play services instead of this app until you tap, refresh or pull down; with "Take it back" roughly 4 of 10 holds fall in the other app's windows and Android's own Buds settings may be stale while the tab is open — the timings are one Play version's. The 1.2.0 known issues stay.

**Not included:** ringing the Case or both buds, firmware updates, choosing the devices of a multipoint connection, anything that needs a Google account.

**Requirements:** Android 14 (API 34) or newer. Tested on a Pixel 9a with GrapheneOS (Android 17) and Buds firmware `release_5.203` only. On any other firmware the app opens in read-only **Safe Mode** and sends no setting changes.

**Install:** download `{APK}` below, allow "Install unknown apps" for your browser or file manager, and open the file. **Updates:** install a newer APK from the Releases page over the old one — it is signed with the same key, so your settings stay. The app never checks for updates itself.

**Verify the download:**
- SHA-256 of the APK: `{APK_SHA256}`
- SHA-256 of the signing certificate: `{CERT_SHA256}` (`apksigner verify --print-certs {APK}`)

**Changes:** see [CHANGELOG.md](https://github.com/tedsluis/opencontrolpixelbudspro2/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md). Third-party licences: `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt` below.

**Risk:** this app sends reverse-engineered commands to your earbuds; use it at your own risk (see the README's "Safety and Safe Mode").

